{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534188-5-phenomenal-realm","id":1534188,"title":"5 Phenomenal Realm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-14T06:19:12-07:00","id":1534188,"title":"5 Phenomenal Realm","content":"Empyrean - The Fallen World Reflection of Aether.<br /> Shadow - The Fallen World Shadow of The Primal Wild.<br /> Underworld - The Fallen World Remnent of Stygia.<br /> Hedge - The Fallen World Ruin of Arcadia.<br /> Inferno - The Fallen World Memory of Pandemonium.<br /> These are the 5 Phenomenal Realm, physical place that were left behide when the Fallen World and The Supernal was seperated.<br /> The Mage whose path match with the Phenomenal realm get Rote to their casting and an 8 again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T07:06:12-07:00","id":1534191,"title":"","content":"This reading has been untrue for well over a decade and two of these realms are either theoretical or inaccessible to anyone wishing to return without needing the power of a god.<br /> <br /> 2e Core provides a mechanical basis for how spells of an aligned Arcanum benefit from being cast in a particular world in its sections on the Underworld, Shadow, and Astral (and Dark Eras 2 added the Hedge to that list), namely that spells of the relevant Subtle Arcanum subtract two dice from their Paradox risk. The Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle introduces the further precedent of using other supernatural energy sources like Glamour or Pyros as Yantras for suitable types of spell and similarly leveraging Rites and Ceremonies toward spells with related effects.<br /> <br /> Also, 8-Again <i>and</i> rote on all spells is overkill as a bonus that can be accessed by Disciple-level spells like Reaching. That's rerolling every initial die that fails once on top of rolling an extra die for every die that succeeds, meaning characters would be at least doubling their spellcasting dicepools for the purposes of getting an exceptional success when we have established tools for making exceptional success easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T07:23:01-07:00","id":1534192,"title":"","content":"I wonder if we would ever have a Realm for Prime Arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T12:55:50-07:00","id":1534209,"title":"","content":"Where do you think God-Machine angels exist? (The are Prime + Fate twilight, right?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T14:02:47-07:00","id":1534210,"title":"","content":"Arcana associations are best-approximations, rather than hard-and-fast correspondences, typically. You do what you want at your table, obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T14:15:42-07:00","id":1534211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534188-5-phenomenal-realm?p=1534209#post1534209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do you think God-Machine angels exist?</div> </div> </div> </div>Earth. The Material Realm. Some of it is what Demon calls facilities, spatial pockets and dimensional folding. But it's not another realm. It's Earth.<br /> <br /> The pat symmetrical realms interpretation is something fans have tried to run with for years and years, and the published books have occasionally gone out of their way to undermine the idea. Some complicating factors:<ul><li>The Empyrean isn't a realm of existence like the other four. Arguably, the Empyrean doesn't <i>exist.</i> It's attested to in vanishingly few published books, never to my recollection with any attestation to anyone having actually visited it or confirmed its existence, or any description of what it is like besides possibly the source of an equal and opposite to the demons of the Inferno. Even Imperial Mysteries, reporting the knowledge of the mightiest sorcerers who hold the greatest cosmic knowledge, great enough to potentially challenge the Exarchs, speaks of the Empyrean only as a postulate with no evidence. It seems to only ever come up in discussions when somebody either wants symmetrical realms to match to the Supernal Realms, or sometimes to create a home realm for Promethean's <i>qashmallim.</i></li> <li>The Inferno isn't a realm of existence like the remaining three. The books are more assertive that the Inferno <i>does</i> exist as a realm, which is a point it has over the Empyrean, but again, we have no attestation to anyone visiting the Inferno and returning to tell any tale, aside from infernal demons who not only lie but seem to have a malleable impression of their own history and origin. Not really somewhere you can go exploring in any comparable way to visiting the Shadow or the Underworld or even the Hedge.</li> <li>Mages who seek ancient history already have an answer for where the Shadow Realm comes from, and it's not the Fall. The Fall happened in a timeline so thoroughly obscured by supernal forces that it effectively never happened within the world's current history, and mages have no real way of figuring when in a hypothetical Time Before it would have occurred, past or future. The Shadow Realm is the result of the Sundering, which did occur in the world's current history, during the Neolithic period. Before that, there was a much more gradated flow between the Material Realm on one extreme and the Spirit Marches on the other.</li> <li>Mages also already know what it looks like when physical parts of the Supernal Realms are left behind, marooned in the Fallen World. They've visited several of them, and some Legacies exist that specialize in one or another. They're called Emanation Realms and finding an iris to one tends to be a lot more work than finding a Shadow locus or an Avernian Gate.</li> </ul>If you want to give corresponding Paths some 8-Again on casting spells while in a realm that thematically resonates with their Path, eh, sure. Call it a special environmental yantra. It's more than I'd do but it wouldn't break much. Giving the rote quality on, what, all spells cast in that realm? is probably too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 04-14-2024, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T15:06:00-07:00","id":1534213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534188-5-phenomenal-realm?p=1534211#post1534211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages who seek ancient history already have an answer for where the Shadow Realm comes from, and it's not the Fall. The Fall happened in a timeline so thoroughly obscured by supernal forces that it effectively never happened within the world's current history, and mages have no real way of figuring when in a hypothetical Time Before it would have occurred, past or future. The Shadow Realm is the result of the Sundering, which did occur in the world's current history, during the Neolithic period. Before that, there was a much more gradated flow between the Material Realm on one extreme and the Spirit Marches on the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shadow existed before the Sundering. The Border Marches existed as a separation between the Shadow and the material world. The Sundering collapsed the Border Marches, and now we have the Gauntlet instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T22:37:39-07:00","id":1534225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534188-5-phenomenal-realm?p=1534213#post1534213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Shadow existed before the Sundering. The Border Marches existed as a separation between the Shadow and the material world. The Sundering collapsed the Border Marches, and now we have the Gauntlet instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand corrected, I remembered this one wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T23:06:46-07:00","id":1534226,"title":"","content":"We have Realm that empower every Subtle Arcanum except for Prime, I hope if Mage ever get a sourcebook on realm invisible they would introduce a Realm for Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T23:59:00-07:00","id":1534230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534188-5-phenomenal-realm?p=1534226#post1534226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have Realm that empower every Subtle Arcanum except for Prime, I hope if Mage ever get a sourcebook on realm invisible they would introduce a Realm for Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since none of the realms are intended to be reflections of the Supernal Realms or the Arcana, and writers go out of their way to not entertain such ideas nowadays, that's quite unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T01:56:49-07:00","id":1534232,"title":"","content":"I contest that the material realms IS the realm of Prime, this is why I brought up G-M angels.<br /> <br /> Magic - of Occult Physics as the G-M calls it - is a natural part of the material realm. It also has Fate, because it is a realm of stories (in the same way Arcadia is Fate/Mind).<br /> <br /> Yes the Shadow and the Material were once easily traversible at all points, you could just wander and find your way into one and back again, similarly you can wander off and get ensnared by a hedge gate... But those seem to he much rarer.<br /> <br /> The Shadow is literally a mirror of the material, two sides of the same coin, despite the Places That Aren't (or however they are called). The Shadow shapes itself based on the Material in a symbolic way. It is not like the Underworld/Arcadia/?? Because the two ARE linked even despite the Sundering.<br /> <br /> The nearest parts of the Hedge are also linked, in some sense, with Hedge paths in industrial areas taking on a distinctly industrial 'theme' (for want of a better word). But they don't depend on the psychic imprint of the material to exist. The Hedge/Arcadia simply are... Even the Underworld exists independently, even if the things that feed it are pulled out of the Material, like a giant trash compactor, crunching through all the detrious left behind. Maybe it exists as a part of the Material even more than the Shadow... Like without things dying the Underworld would be nothing (but perhaps the Sea of Fragments - without the Fragments - and maybe the Chthonic entities residing there...).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T02:42:11-07:00","id":1534235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534188-5-phenomenal-realm?p=1534230#post1534230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Since none of the realms are intended to be reflections of the Supernal Realms or the Arcana, and writers go out of their way to not entertain such ideas nowadays, that's quite unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>It give the 4 other path realm advantage that Obrimos alone doesn't get to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T03:05:47-07:00","id":1534236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534188-5-phenomenal-realm?p=1534235#post1534235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It give the 4 other path realm advantage that Obrimos alone doesn't get to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>An advantage that is<br /> 1.) Not Path-exclusive since it only requires having the subtle Arcanum; anyone can learn any of the other four, including Obrimoi.<br /> 2.) Limited to a specific realm that the mage might not even be interested in. Just because you have a few dots of Fate doesn't mean you'll ever enter the Hedge. In fact, if you don't have Fate at all, you'll likely not develop any relevant Obsessions regarding the Hedge anyway.<br /> 3.) Honestly quite minor; -2 Paradox dice is nice but most of the time you don't roll Paradox, and the times you do, you can buy it down by the exact same amount by spending 2 Mana instead.<br /> <br /> Wanting a Prime-adjacent realm to &quot;balance&quot; Obrimos is just wanting symmetry for the sake of symmetry, which by itself would be a terrible reason to introduce a whole new realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T07:07:25-07:00","id":1534247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534188-5-phenomenal-realm?p=1534235#post1534235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It give the 4 other path realm advantage that Obrimos alone doesn't get to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean the ability to use spells to travel to other realms and affect ephemeral entities, all things are not equal. Spell travel to the Hedge or the Astral Realm is not of the same ease and utility as spell travel to the Shadow or the Underworld (I'd argue the Underworld isn't of the same utility as the Shadow either), nor are spells to affect goetia. Conversely, there's a whole lot more non-ephemeral stuff to do with the other Arcana that aren't Death and Spirit.<br /> <br /> Balance and symmetry aren't the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T20:15:17-07:00","id":1534280,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I do not think that ascribing each Supernal Realm a corresponding Phenomenal Realm is a good idea. For that matter, the Supernal itself seems to have the character of positive existence, and thus appears to be within phenomenal existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-16T02:40:19-07:00","id":1534292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534188-5-phenomenal-realm?p=1534280#post1534280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that matter, the Supernal itself seems to have the character of positive existence, and thus appears to be within phenomenal existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Phenomenal' is a term of art within the setting to mean something that's a part of the Fallen World. Both <i>Imperial Mysteries</i> and <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> give alternative reasons why you'd use the term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-16T12:58:57-07:00","id":1534301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534188-5-phenomenal-realm?p=1534292#post1534292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'Phenomenal' is a term of art within the setting to mean something that's a part of the Fallen World. Both <i>Imperial Mysteries</i> and <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> give alternative reasons why you'd use the term.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware of that. That is why I specifically mentioned phenomenal existence rather than the Phenomenal Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T12:28:21-07:00","id":1534959,"title":"","content":"Back in the early days of 1e, I took up the head canon that the physical world itself was the shadow of Aether. After all, it is the one that is constantly awash in solar radiation, pounded by tumultuous storms, covered in a network of electrical cabling, and sprinkled with ley lines and hallows.<br /> <br /> I don't know if anything in 2e would invalidate that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T06:22:26-07:00","id":1534995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534188-5-phenomenal-realm?p=1534959#post1534959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if anything in 2e would invalidate that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that an Obrimos can use Mage Sight to see the Aether no matter where they are and the presentation of Supernal Realms as more frameworks created by the Watchtowers might.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}